      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="timeline">A realistic timeline</h2>
  <p>
    There is no single honest number here, and any roadmap that gives you an exact week count is guessing.
    What is true across most people who make this switch: the business-fluency and analytics layer takes
    real time to build if you are starting from zero, user research and framework practice can happen in
    parallel with that, and the case study step usually cannot be rushed without producing something shallow
    enough that an interviewer sees through it in the first two follow-up questions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some people who already sit close to product work — a business analyst, a technical program manager, a
    designer already influencing a roadmap — get interview-ready in a focused stretch of a few months. Others
    building business fluency, analytics comfort, and a first real case study from a completely unrelated
    background more realistically need closer to a year. Judge your own pace against the build order above,
    not against someone else's LinkedIn timeline post.
  </p>

