  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>
  <p>
    Do not open one more product management course before you have picked your entry path and named the one
    real decision you are going to turn into a case study. That single choice does more for your odds than
    another week of watching framework videos.
  </p>
  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>Pick your entry path from the three above based on what you already have access to, not on prestige.</p>
    <p>Then start at step one of the build order: business and domain fluency, before any tool or certificate.</p>
  </div>
  <p>
    Moving toward earlier financial freedom through this roadmap comes down to the same thing it always
    does: the right skill mix, visible proof, and clear communication, stacked deliberately rather than
    collected at random. If you want a second opinion on whether product management fits your specific
    situation, <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
